    {
      "id": "claim_e037b5cd462545b5b823e18e8fc0b291",
      "statement": "The capital model rolls CET1 forward each quarter as prior CET1 plus net income minus preferred dividends, common dividends and buybacks plus other movements. It compounds RWA by a quarterly growth rate, and common dividends depend on a share count reduced by buybacks divided by the assumed share price.",
