      "statement": "A 200 bp parallel fall reduces 12-month NII by 3,016.89 (-6.01%) from 50,236.91 to 47,220.02, within the 7.0% Board limit. Symmetric shocks give the mirrored values for +200 and +/-100 (+/-1,508.44, 3.00%), because the model is linear and betas are constant across shock sizes.",
